1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
The Screws

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,080
Hey, Tom Thomas!

3
00:00:08,359 --> 00:00:09,480
What are you thinking about? Huh?

4
00:00:10,359 --> 00:00:12,200
For school I have to write an essay.

5
00:00:12,359 --> 00:00:13,679
My very best friend.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,519
I don't know. Who should I write about?

7
00:00:15,519 --> 00:00:16,640
What do you mean who?

8
00:00:16,719 --> 00:00:18,160
Aren't I your closest friend?

9
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,000
Of course!

10
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,839
How could I forget to write about you?

11
00:00:20,839 --> 00:00:22,359
And you can keep forgetting!

12
00:00:22,559 --> 00:00:24,160
That's our secret, right?

13
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:27,320
Don't you remember the promise you made when we met?

14
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:30,320
Hmm, sure, how could I forget?

15
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:39,320
What's wrong with Chewsocka today?

16
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:48,320
Chewsocka, why are these screws bothering you so badly?

17
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,700
What's with you? Leave them alone already!

18
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,100
Will you just calm down?

19
00:01:08,200 --> 00:01:10,500
You're going to destroy my plane!

20
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,500
Let's get out of here!

21
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:26,700
What's going on?

22
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:32,500
What's going on?

23
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:38,500
Hey, if you don't turn back again, I'm not letting you go.

24
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,400
Oh, please, don't be afraid. I'm not going to hurt you, too.

25
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:46,900
I'll just ask you one question and let you go.

26
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:51,319
Nolik!

27
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:52,319
We can't!

28
00:01:52,559 --> 00:01:53,879
Don't worry about it.

29
00:01:54,279 --> 00:01:55,479
Quit your staring!

30
00:01:55,599 --> 00:01:57,000
Ask your question, boy!

31
00:01:57,119 --> 00:01:59,039
No way you can talk!

32
00:01:59,239 --> 00:02:02,079
Just… just… just tell me, who are you?

33
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:04,359
Fixies!

34
00:02:04,519 --> 00:02:07,560
That's all! We answered! Now you… let us out!

35
00:02:07,639 --> 00:02:10,199
Oh, wait! But what's it mean that you're Fixies?

36
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:12,240
That's already question number two!

37
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:14,280
You promised to let us out, didn't you?

38
00:02:14,519 --> 00:02:15,560
I'm sorry.

39
00:02:16,079 --> 00:02:17,479
You can leave now.

40
00:02:17,959 --> 00:02:19,519
Simka, it's fine.

41
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:22,200
I can see from his look that we can trust him.

42
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:26,120
Uh, alright, we'll tell him.

43
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:30,360
You gotta swear that you don't tell anyone else!

44
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,439
I swear it!

45
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:34,840
Fixies

46
00:02:35,360 --> 00:02:40,200
We're the little people that live inside of machines and appliances and take care of them,

47
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:43,200
fixing them, cleaning them and oiling them.

48
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:45,120
Humans never suspect us.

49
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:48,840
They think that if something breaks and then suddenly starts working again,

50
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:50,840
that it happened all by itself.

51
00:02:51,039 --> 00:02:53,439
Well, nothing happens by itself!

52
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:57,439
It happens because we, the Fixies, are living inside.

53
00:02:57,680 --> 00:03:03,199
Yes, without the Fixies, humans would have so many more problems with their machines.

54
00:03:04,719 --> 00:03:06,080
That's awesome!

55
00:03:06,599 --> 00:03:08,199
And so what are your names?

56
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,960
That's already question number three.

57
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,800
You can call me Nolik and her name is Simka.

58
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,599
And my name is Tom Thomas. Will you come back over?

59
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,840
Oh well.

60
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:31,360
Uh, I was this close to becoming the first kid in the whole world to make friends with the Fixies.

61
00:03:33,719 --> 00:03:36,560
I thought you guys would never come back over.

62
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:39,000
And we didn't plan on coming back.

63
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:42,560
But then we thought it would be really great to be the only Fixies in the whole world

64
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:45,000
who are friends with the only kid in the whole world

65
00:03:45,199 --> 00:03:46,800
who is friends with the Fixies!

66
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:50,520
And who has told no one about us!

67
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:57,680
The Fixies do everything they can do to hide from humans.

68
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,920
They are afraid that if humans discovered Fixies,

69
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,360
they would hunt them down and capture them,

70
00:04:03,439 --> 00:04:06,480
and start keeping them in cages just like pets.

71
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:08,040
And worse than that,

72
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:12,960
they would take them into their laboratories and start examining them under microscopes,

73
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:16,439
even conducting scientific experiments on them.

74
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:20,240
Or suppose that humans thought we'd do all their work for them,

75
00:04:20,319 --> 00:04:24,759
and so they decided that they didn't have to take care of their appliances any longer.

76
00:04:25,879 --> 00:04:27,879
Well then, let me tell you this.

77
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:32,600
If humans decided that they didn't have to clean or fix their own appliances, then

78
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:36,800
not even the Fixies will be able to stop them from breaking no matter what they do!

79
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:41,759
That's why the Fixies are very smart to hide from humans.

80
00:04:43,884 --> 00:04:47,759
Okay, then, I'll write about someone else.

81
00:04:47,759 --> 00:04:54,917
I have the very best friend ever.

82
00:04:54,917 --> 00:04:56,322
Period.

83
00:04:56,322 --> 00:04:59,674
When something's broken, he repairs it.

84
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:02,935
He's the one and only Nol...

85
00:05:02,935 --> 00:05:07,136
The one and only Nolan!
